    "description": "Cast Brass Double Inkstand\nBrass Double Inkwell Desk Stand with Pen Tray\nRenaissance Revival Style, Late 19th to Early 20th Century\nThis ornate cast brass desk inkstand exemplifies the historicist decorative motifs of late 19th-century Renaissance Revival design. The composition features an arched openwork pediment with winged cherubs flanking a central crest, set above two inkwells and an integrated pen tray centered with a bearded Green Man grotesque mask. Complete with its two removable brass ink cups and domed finial lids, it combines functional writing utility with ornate sculptural presence.\nHeavy cast brass construction weighing 3.6 lbs with authentic sand-cast underside\nComplete 5-piece assembly including desk stand, two brass well cups, and two domed lids\nDetailed casting with winged cherubs, scrolling side handles, and a Green Man motif\nMeasures approximately 10 inches wide by 7 inches deep and 4.5 inches high\nCondition:\nVery good vintage condition with intact structural integrity and all original components present. Shows an attractive natural brass patina with light oxidation and surface darkening in recessed areas consistent with age. No cracks, breaks, or repairs observed; sits level on its feet.",
